  Best I could come up with was enhanced skill level reducing 
failure rates enough to permit casting while wearing a small 
shield.  Of course, divination spells don't generally affect
combat directly anyway.  

  Those that do (detect monster, magic mapping, clairvoyance, 
light, etc.) can be cast beforehand without a shield.  Then
the shield can be worn for battle.

  Detect monster starts lasting more than one turn at the 
"skilled" skill level.

  So once again, no motivation for enhancing divination spell 
skill past "skilled."


  And enhancing a spell skill from "skilled" to "Expert" takes 
two skill slots (instead of the one slot from Basic->Skilled).
So this looks like a good place to save two skill slots.


