  In the above diagrams, character at position 'X' could use
the jumping spell at that skill level to reach any of the squares 
marked '*', given lit target square and no obstructions.

  (Jumping boots range footprint corresponds to unskilled spell
of jumping.)

  Rogue and Tourists can get to skilled in Escape spells.
  Wizards can get to Expert.

  Potion/spell/boots of speed and Expert jumping spell lets
you travel four times as fast as "very fast" by itself.
Should easily average three times as fast.  And you can wear
speed boots.  (That should warm the cockles of your hearts.)

  The biggest problem will be having a lit landing space.
No problem on Medusa or the Castle.  (Expert skill guarantees
crossing Medusa with the spell of jump?)

  Expert escape skill can jump across the Castle or Ludios 
moat and never be in range of an eel/kraken.

  Safe crossing of the Fort Ludios moat will require spell/
wand/scroll of light.

  Juiblex level and the Astral Plane still require light source.

  Plane of Fire gets interesting.  Lava squares are regarded
as 'lit', I do believe.  (Also useful for the Skilled+ spells
of cone of cold and fireball.  Although cone of cold can only
use a lava square as a target *once*.)  

  Requires fireproof water walking boots.  (Suddenly the lava 
is useful!)  Spell of jumping should then be much safer than 
using jumping boots on the Plane of Fire.


  Escape when mobbed then becomes: zap wand of light, zap wand
of teleport, spell of jump.  Mana cost of the spell of jump
looks like 5 without the AoY, 5-15 with the Amulet of Yendor.

  On Astral, zapping wand of light as you go seems an excellent
idea (you may have to come back, after all).

  And now you can *really* move at warp speed around the temple
in Moloch's Sanctum, zapping wands of teleport, light, secret door 
detection as needed.  Or even use the spells of teleport away, 
light, and detect unseen.  (You won't have the AoY yet, after 
all.)


 Light sources:

  Sunsword has a light footprint of radius two, or thereabouts.
Jumping boots and unskilled spell of jump both outrange it.

  Lanterns, candles, oil/magic lamps lighting footprint corresponds 
to the 'basic' skill level jumping footprint.  As best as I can 
recollect at this point.  The tool spoiler doesn't seem to say.

  The spell/wand of light has a footprint of radius 5, but will
cost another turn.  Blessed scroll of light has radius 9: Enough
for two full length Expert skill level jumps in a straight line.



